meta {
  name: 9j. Discovery API forward-guard (#1379, PENDING)
  type: http
  seq: 31
}

get {
  url: {{apisixApiUrl}}/v1/datasets/{{sagaDataSetId}}/apis
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

tests {
  // FORWARD GUARD for the deferred discovery endpoint GET /v1/datasets/{id}/apis (#1379/#1362).
  // It is intentionally inert until discovery is built: set env var `discoveryEnabled: true` while
  // implementing discovery and these assertions become the acceptance gate. They are designed to
  // FAIL on the three classic discovery mistakes (see docs).
  const enabled = bru.getEnvVar('discoveryEnabled') === 'true';

  if (!enabled) {
    test("Discovery API (#1379) is pending — set discoveryEnabled=true to activate this guard", function() {
      expect(true).to.equal(true);
    });
  } else {
    test("Discovery is NOT swallowed by the FROST /v1/datasets/{id}/* route (not 404)", function() {
      // A 404 means the dedicated higher-priority /v1/datasets/*/apis carve-out route is missing
      // or mis-prioritised, so the dynamic FROST route caught /apis.
      expect(res.getStatus()).to.not.equal(404);
    });

    test("Authorized discovery request succeeds (200, not 403)", function() {
      // A 403 means OPA is missing the /v1/datasets/{id}/apis GET -> DATASET_READ mapping
      // (authz/rego/data/backends/portal_backend/data.json).
      expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
    });

    test("Returns the named-API list as an array, not a FROST SensorThings document", function() {
      // FROST's root returns an object with a `value` array of entity-set links. The discovery
      // endpoint must return the dataset's named APIs as an array — this catches a routing
      // collision that reached FROST instead of portal-backend.
      expect(res.body).to.be.an('array');
      expect(res.body).to.not.have.property('value');
    });

    test("Discovery list includes the dataset's named API slug 'things'", function() {
      const slugs = (res.body || []).map(a => a.slug);
      expect(slugs).to.include('things');
    });
  }
}

docs {
  **Saga step 9j of 18 — FORWARD GUARD (discovery API, #1379 — currently DEFERRED).**

  The discovery endpoint `GET /v1/datasets/{id}/apis` is intentionally out of scope for #1368 but reserved for: it lists a dataset's named APIs. This step is a guard that stays **green and inert** today (one placeholder assertion) and turns into the **acceptance gate** the moment someone implements discovery — flip `discoveryEnabled: true` in the environment.

  It fails on the three classic discovery mistakes:
  1. **Routing collision** — the dynamic FROST route `/v1/datasets/{id}/*` swallows `/apis`. Needs a dedicated higher-priority APISIX route `/v1/datasets/*/apis` → portal-backend. Detected via 404 / a FROST-shaped (object with `value`) response instead of an array.
  2. **Missing OPA permission** — `/v1/datasets/{id}/apis` GET not mapped to `DATASET_READ` in `authz/rego/data/backends/portal_backend/data.json` (+ a `portal_backend_test.rego` case). Detected via 403.
  3. **Wrong contract** — not returning the named-API list (array including the known slug `things`).

  **Reserved slug:** `apis` is already reserved (frontend `RESERVED_SLUGS`, backend `NamedApiAllowedSlugValidator`) so no named API can shadow this path — that guard is active today (see ApiConfigForm Vitest test).

  **Precondition (when enabled):** released dataset with named API `things` (steps 4-9); bearer token has DATASET_READ.

  **Expected (when enabled):** 200 OK, JSON array of named APIs including slug `things`.
}
